:: Africa Q4 study {"position":"1400,2120","size":"100,100"}
(set: $tries to 0)
*History:* The wichi — a ritual specialist — wore this type of mask, and the act of donning and removing it was carried out in secrecy. This concealment was integral to the mask's authority: the wearer disappeared behind it, allowing the mask itself to represent a force beyond any individual.

[[Finish region->Africa Done]]



