[[Next->Americas Q2]]



:: Americas Q1 study {"position":"550,575","size":"100,100"}
(set: $tries to 0)
*History:* The potlatch is a ceremonial feast at which the host gives away great quantities of wealth. Guests witness and thereby validate the host's status, inherited names, and rights — a form of living record in an oral culture.

[[Continue->Americas Q2]]



:: Americas Q2 {"position":"300,700","size":"100,100"}

*Burton gestures toward the museum label.*
**Question 2 of 4: This mask was made by the Kwakwaka'wakw of the Northwest Coast and collected for a foreign museum. During much of the period when masks like this were being gathered, the ceremony they belonged to was:**

(link: "Actively promoted by the Canadian government as a tourist attraction")[ (goto: "Americas Q2 no") ]

(link: "Banned by the Canadian government for decades — a suppression that is part of why so many of these masks ended up in museums far from their communities")[ (goto: "Americas Q2 ok") ]

(link: "Permitted, but restricted by Indigenous law to the summer months only")[ (goto: "Americas Q2 no") ]

(link: "Performed only for European traders, in exchange for goods")[ (goto: "Americas Q2 no") ]


:: Americas Q2 no {"position":"300,825","size":"100,100"}
(set: $tries to $tries + 1)
(if: $tries >= 2)[
*Burton:* "Not to worry — being wrong is part of the journey. Here is the answer."

(text-style: "bold")[Right answer: A Canadian government ban on the potlatch ceremony, which forced the confiscation and dispersal of ceremonial items.]

(link: "STUDY THE INFORMATION")[ (set: $tries to 0) (goto: "Americas Q2 study") ]
(link: "MOVE ON TO THE NEXT QUESTION")[ (set: $tries to 0) (goto: "Americas Q3") ]
](else:)[
*Burton:* "Not quite. Look at the evidence again."
[[Try again->Americas Q2]]
]



:: Americas Q2 ok {"position":"175,825","size":"100,100"}
(set: $tries to 0)
(set: $score to it + 10)

Correct! It was a major policy of cultural assimilation.

[[Next->Americas Q3]]



:: Americas Q2 study {"position":"425,825","size":"100,100"}
(set: $tries to 0)
*History:* Canada banned the potlatch from 1885 to 1951. During this period authorities confiscated ceremonial objects, many of which entered museum collections abroad — which is why so many masks are now far from their communities of origin.

[[Continue->Americas Q3]]



