[[Next->China Q3]]



:: China Q2 study {"position":"800,1125","size":"100,100"}
(set: $tries to 0)
*History:* Glazing means applying a layer of glass-forming minerals to the clay surface, which fuses in the kiln to create a hard, shiny, waterproof coating. The fahua technique uses raised clay outlines to contain separate pools of coloured glaze, like stained glass.

[[Continue to Question 3->China Q3]]



