:: China Q3 study {"position":"800,1375","size":"100,100"}
(set: $tries to 0)
*History:* Cloisonné enamel was among the most prized luxury arts of imperial China. Objects like this jar were made for the palace as ceremonial vessels or display pieces, broadcasting the wealth, taste, and power of the imperial court.

[[Continue to Question 4->China Q4]]



