*History:* The Xuande reign (1426–1435) falls within the Ming dynasty and is celebrated as a golden age for imperial craft. Some of the earliest securely dated high-quality cloisonné enamel pieces survive from this period, making them especially important for art historians.

[[Finish region->China Done]]



